<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Theban Eleventh Dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">2134 BCE – 2055 BCE (approx.) · capital Thebes</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Theban kings who rose from local governors to reunite Egypt at the end of the First Intermediate Period.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 2134 BCE the governors of the Theban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nome">nome</a>, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mentuhotep-i">Mentuhotep I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/intef-i">Intef I</a>, broke with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/herakleopolitan-kingdom">Herakleopolitan Kingdom</a> and claimed royal titles. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>, until then a minor provincial town, became the capital of a southern kingdom stretching from Elephantine to the region of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/abydos">Abydos</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/intef-ii">Intef II</a>, who reigned for about fifty years, fought the north for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thinis">Thinis</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/abydos">Abydos</a> and expanded the kingdom. The early kings were buried in large rock-cut 'saff' tombs at el-Tarif on the west bank of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>. They promoted the war god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montu">Montu</a> and the local god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a>, and relied on Nubian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archery">archers</a>, some of whom settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gebelein">Gebelein</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mentuhotep-ii">Mentuhotep II</a>, who came to the throne around 2055 BCE, a date often used for the start of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/middle-kingdom-of-egypt">Middle Kingdom of Egypt</a>, later defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herakleopolis-magna">Herakleopolis</a> and reunited the country. His mortuary temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deir-el-bahari">Deir el-Bahari</a> set a model for later Theban royal building.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 2134 BCE – 2055 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:17.23%;width:1.57%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>2134 BCE – 2055 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/22nd-century-bce">22nd century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century-bce">21st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thebes</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Intef I, Intef II, Mentuhotep II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Early Eleventh Dynasty, Theban kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-2094&amp;focus=theban-eleventh-dynasty" aria-label="Theban Eleventh Dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5543 1232 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Theban Eleventh Dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5863 1488L5807 1370M5863 1488L5813 1353"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5807 1370h0M5813 1353h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5863 1488h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5863 1488h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Thebes. <a href="/atlas?year=-2094&amp;focus=theban-eleventh-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
